  "notes": "USAGE:\nDistinct from {沸|わ}く (to boil), which is a homophone. {湧|わ}く refers to things emerging from the ground or arising spontaneously, while {沸|わ}く refers to liquid reaching boiling point or a crowd getting excited.\n\nOften used with the compound {湧|わ}き{出|で}る (to gush out, to spring forth) for emphasis.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {温泉|おんせん}が{湧|わ}く: hot spring water wells up\n- {興味|きょうみ}が{湧|わ}く: interest arises\n- やる{気|き}が{湧|わ}く: motivation wells up\n- {勇気|ゆうき}が{湧|わ}く: courage surges",
